# Bugfix TDD Rule

For every bug fix, use a regression-first TDD flow on top of the general Detroit TDD rule.

## Mandatory Sequence

1. Reproduce the bug with an automated test.
2. Confirm the test fails for the current behavior.
3. Implement the smallest fix to make the test pass.
4. Run related suite to ensure no regressions.
5. Refactor safely with all tests green.

## Regression Test Requirements

- The test must capture user-visible incorrect behavior.
- Name tests by defect scenario: `should_<expected>_when_<bug_condition>`.
- Include at least one nearby edge case if the bug is boundary-related.
- Do not delete the regression test after fixing the bug.
- Reproduce the bug at the highest useful public boundary first.

## Fix Scope Rules

- Fix the root cause, not only symptoms.
- Keep changes minimal and focused on the defect scope.
- Avoid broad refactors before the bug is green.
- If behavior changes intentionally, update tests to match new contract.

## Verification Checklist

- Regression test is red before fix and green after fix.
- Existing related tests remain green.
- No new warnings/errors introduced by the fix.
- Commit message should mention bug scenario and protected behavior.
